    {
      "id": "gv-786134-b00001",
      "text": "Since the beginning of the year, there has been a steep rise in the price of market goods in Madagascar. The Malagasy people are hesitant to speak out about this, and they remain resilient. However, the country's high cost of living still requires a government response.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 1,
      "body_start": 0,
      "body_end": 270,
      "source_links": [
        "https://2424.mg/situation-economique-acceleration-de-linflation-a-115-pour-madagascar-au-mois-de-janvier-2023/",
        "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Madagascar",
        "https://www.rfi.fr/fr/afrique/20230215-madagascar-forte-hausse-des-prix-%C3%A0-la-consommation-pour-les-m%C3%A9nages"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-786134-b00002",
      "text": "By August 2022, the rate of inflation had already reached 9.3 percent. According to economists from the National Institute of Statistics (INSTAT), this is likely to increase further this year. In fact, since January, there has been a significant rise in the cost of foodstuff. In one week alone, the cost of 1 kg (2.2 lb) of rice increased from MGA 3,200 (USD 0.7373) to MGA 3,600 (USD 0.8294). Today’s cost is MGA 4,100 (USD 0.9446).",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 2,
      "body_start": 272,
      "body_end": 706,
      "source_links": [
        "https://actu.orange.mg/un-taux-dinflation-a-93-selon-linstat/",
        "https://madagascar-tribune.com/Le-kilo-du-riz-franchit-la-barre-de-4-000-ariary.html",
        "https://www.linfo.re/ochttps:/madagascar-tribune.com/Le-kilo-du-riz-franchit-la-barre-de-4-000-ariary.htmlean-indien/madagascar/madagascar-le-prix-du-riz-flambe-dans-la-grande-ile"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-786134-b00003",
      "text": "Rice is a prominent feature of the Malagasy diet. Life is strongly dependent upon rice; it is not only a staple food, but also a vital component of Malagasy culture and philosophy. As the saying goes, “It is only with rice that we can be full.”",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 3,
      "body_start": 708,
      "body_end": 952,
      "source_links": [
        "https://fr.malagasy-tours.com/que-mangent-les-malgaches/",
        "https://lekanto.com/les-habitudes-alimentaires-malgaches/",
        "https://maison-de-madagascar.ch/tout-sur-madagascar/le-riz-aliment-roi-de-madagascar/"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-786134-b00004",
      "text": "However, few households are currently able to buy the food they require. Eighty-one percent of the population is living below the poverty line and thereby have to tighten their belts even further. Most people have had to reduce their spending, and some end up going hungry. Even the middle-income strata have been significantly affected. They, too, are having to take cost-saving actions.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 4,
      "body_start": 954,
      "body_end": 1342,
      "source_links": [
        "https://la1ere.francetvinfo.fr/reunion/madagascar-81-de-la-population-vit-sous-le-seuil-de-pauvrete-1288848.html",
        "https://midi-madagasikara.mg/2023/03/23/flambee-des-prix-du-riz-vent-de-revolte-chez-les-consommateurs/"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-786134-b00005",
      "text": "A ban on public protests",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 5,
      "body_start": 1344,
      "body_end": 1368,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "h3",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-786134-b00006",
      "text": "Most people now realize that holding protests will not resolve the country’s inflation issues. After all, the government has recently limited citizens’ right to protest, under the pretext of the country being in a pre-election period:",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 6,
      "body_start": 1370,
      "body_end": 1604,
      "source_links": [
        "https://www.impact.sn/Madagascar-a-sept-mois-de-la-presidentielle-le-gouvernement-restreint-le-droit-de-manifester_a37654.html"
      ],
      "source_kind": "div",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-786134-b00007",
      "text": "> Ce vendredi 31 mars au soir, à la télévision nationale malgache, le ministre de l’intérieur a annoncé que toutes les manifestations à caractère politique dans un lieu public sont désormais interdites et devront se tenir uniquement dans un endroit clos afin « de préserver l’ordre public ».",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 7,
      "body_start": 1606,
      "body_end": 1897,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "blockquote",
      "source_is_quotation": true
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-786134-b00008",
      "text": "> On the evening of Friday, March 31, the Malagasy Minister of the Interior, announced on national television that all political protests in public places had been banned. They should only be held in enclosed areas ‘to maintain public order’.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 8,
      "body_start": 1899,
      "body_end": 2141,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "blockquote",
      "source_is_quotation": true
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-786134-b00009",
      "text": "In November 2023, the Malagasy people will go to the polls to elect their new president. However, the socio-political landscape is already tense. On March 7, the authorities broke up protests held by students from the Polytechnic Higher School of Vontovorona, where there were violent confrontations with the security forces. Subsequently, on March 31, the Minister of the Interior, Cécile Manorohanta, announced a ban on all political protests and meetings in public places, with the exception of members of the executive.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 9,
      "body_start": 2143,
      "body_end": 2666,
      "source_links": [
        "https://lexpress.mg/08/03/2023/manifestation-vontovorona-violents-affrontements-entre-etudiants-et-forces-de-lordre/",
        "https://www.linfo.re/ocean-indien/madagascar/madagascar-l-etat-interdit-les-reunions-politiques-en-plein-air-de-tous-les-partis",
        "https://www.linfo.re/ocean-indien/madagascar/madagascar-la-ceni-devoile-les-dates-de-l-election-presidentielle-2023"
      ],
      "source_kind": "div",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-786134-b00010",
      "text": "Causes of inflation",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 10,
      "body_start": 2668,
      "body_end": 2687,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "h3",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-786134-b00011",
      "text": "Adverse weather conditions and the disrepair of its road networks both significantly affect the cost of certain products. Madagascar is economically dependent on foreign imports of basic commodities because of its inability to produce enough supplies to sustain its population of almost 27 million inhabitants. This is also attributable to a lack of market price awareness and control by state officials.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 11,
      "body_start": 2689,
      "body_end": 3093,
      "source_links": [
        "https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/D%C3%A9mographie_de_Madagascar",
        "https://laverite.mg/politique/item/14110-consommation-l%E2%80%99importation-de-ppn-reste-incontournable.html",
        "https://midi-madagasikara.mg/2023/01/09/infrastructures-menaces-de-coupures-des-routes-nationales/",
        "https://theconversation.com/face-au-changement-climatique-les-agricultures-africaines-au-defi-de-la-securite-alimentaire-156770",
        "https://www.madagascar-tribune.com/Prix-des-PPN-le-ministere-du-commerce-renforce-les-controles.html"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-786134-b00012",
      "text": "The country’s economy is also exposed to unfavorable global economic circumstances, which have been hit hard by inflation because of the Russia-Ukraine war. As Ukraine supplied 30 percent of the world’s wheat, the cost of this basic agricultural commodity shot up following Russia’s invasion of Ukraine in February 2022.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 12,
      "body_start": 3095,
      "body_end": 3415,
      "source_links": [
        "https://globalvoices.org/special/russia-invades-ukraine/",
        "https://theconversation.com/envol-des-prix-insecurite-alimentaire-les-lourdes-consequences-pour-lafrique-de-la-guerre-en-ukraine-181193",
        "https://www.la-croix.com/Monde/Ukraine-Chaque-annee-74-ble-produit-pays-partent-letranger-2022-03-11-1201204466"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-786134-b00013",
      "text": "According to Benoît Faivre-Dupaigre, a researcher at the Economic Analysis and Public Policy Department of the French Development Agency (AFD), food security in Africa is anything but stable. This is the continent where food aid is most required. Based on this report, Madagascar, the Central African Republic and the Democratic Republic of Congo (DRC) are the three African countries most at risk.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 13,
      "body_start": 3417,
      "body_end": 3815,
      "source_links": [
        "https://www.france24.com/fr/afrique/20230113-r%C3%A9siliente-face-au-covid-19-l-%C3%A9conomie-africaine-p%C3%A9nalis%C3%A9e-par-la-guerre-en-ukraine",
        "https://www.lejdd.fr/international/en-afrique-le-dilemme-dune-securite-alimentaire-soutenable-133167"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-786134-b00014",
      "text": "The following report by the German international broadcaster Deutsche Welle shows how various climatic and political factors have contributed to this major crisis:",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 14,
      "body_start": 3817,
      "body_end": 3980,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-786134-b00015",
      "text": "Basic commodities price hike",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 15,
      "body_start": 3982,
      "body_end": 4010,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "h3",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-786134-b00016",
      "text": "The cost of everyday essentials is on the rise, as shown in the table below, which lists the products affected by this price hike:",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 16,
      "body_start": 4012,
      "body_end": 4142,
      "source_links": [
        "https://web.facebook.com/lysan.rabenjamina/posts/pfbid0M7c2SAw72o7as37usSdwZPtsb6a5yxVxKRa2BREndWBgWjDBXUEX4suiuh935YGgl"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-786134-b00017",
      "text": "Est-ce que ça va continuer?",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 17,
      "body_start": 4144,
      "body_end": 4171,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "tr",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-786134-b00018",
      "text": "La dette que le peuple et ses descendants doivent payer s'élèvent à 4 milliard de dollars",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 18,
      "body_start": 4173,
      "body_end": 4262,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
